- content_for :title, "Add New Goals"

- content_for :header do
  Add New Goals

.container-fluid.py-4
  - unless @subject_is_current_user
    - subject_name = @subject_teammate.person&.casual_name.presence || @subject_teammate.person&.display_name || 'this teammate'
    .alert.alert-info.mb-4
      Creating goals in context for
      %strong= subject_name
      — Personal defaults to them. Team and department defaults use their memberships.

  %p.text-muted.mb-4
    Choose who the goal(s) will belong to, then whether you are creating one goal or several at once.
    Your choice pre-selects the owner on the next page.

  .row.g-4
    - @create_scopes.each do |scope|
      .col-md-6
        .card.h-100
          .card-body.d-flex.flex-column
            .d-flex.align-items-start.gap-3.mb-3
              %i.bi.display-6.text-primary{class: scope[:icon]}
              %div
                %h3.mb-1= scope[:label]
                %p.text-muted.mb-0= scope[:description]

            - if scope[:owner_label].present?
              .border.rounded.bg-light.px-3.py-2.mb-3
                %div.small.text-muted.mb-1 Default owner
                .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2
                  - record = scope[:owner_record]
                  - if record.is_a?(CompanyTeammate)
                    = teammate_profile_image(record, size: 40)
                  - elsif record.present?
                    = group_avatar(record, size: 40)
                  %span.fw-semibold.fs-5= scope[:owner_label]

            - if scope[:hint].present?
              %p.small.text-muted.mb-3
                %i.bi.bi-info-circle.me-1
                = scope[:hint]

            .mt-auto.d-flex.flex-wrap.gap-2
              - link_params = {}
              - link_params[:owner_id] = scope[:owner_id] if scope[:owner_id].present?
              - link_params[:return_url] = @return_url if @return_url.present?
              - link_params[:return_text] = @return_text if @return_text.present?
              = link_to new_organization_goal_path(@organization, link_params), class: "btn btn-primary" do
                %i.bi.bi-plus-lg.me-1
                Single goal
              = link_to bulk_new_organization_goals_path(@organization, link_params), class: "btn btn-outline-primary" do
                %i.bi.bi-plus-lg.me-1
                Multiple goals at once
              - if scope[:key] == :team && scope[:owner_id].blank?
                = link_to my_teams_organization_path(@organization), class: "btn btn-outline-secondary" do
                  %i.bi.bi-people.me-1
                  My Teams

  %p.small.text-muted.mt-4.mb-0
    %i.bi.bi-info-circle.me-1
    You can change the owner of a goal when editing the goals.
